#usda 1.0
(
    """Put the YAM's base frame on the underside of its base, where I2RT puts it.

    MuJoCo Menagerie's yam.xml (71f066ad) comes from I2RT's first published
    model (i2rt-robotics/i2rt@180dc6d, 2025-08), whose base frame sits 10 mm
    above the bottom face of the base: the base mesh spans z = -10.0 .. 63.1 mm
    in the `arm` body, and joint1's origin is at 63.1 mm. I2RT re-origined the
    YAM on its Onshape CAD in v1.2.4 (#46, i2rt@5d47b35) and every release since
    (v1.4.0, i2rt@fe78bae) keeps it there: the same 73.1 mm base mesh spans
    0 .. 73.1 mm, joint1 is at 68.0 mm and the shoulder (joint2) axis is
    113.5 mm above the frame (DH d1 = 0.1135 in robot_models/arm/yam/v1/README.md).

    A consumer that stands the base frame on its mounting surface -- I2RT's
    convention, and every YAM station built from I2RT's models -- otherwise
    sinks the base 10 mm into the surface and carries the whole arm 10 mm low.

    This layer moves the frame, nothing else: everything the `arm` body owns
    (its visual mesh, its collider, its centre of mass and the link_1 subtree
    with joint1's anchor) rises 10 mm in that body's frame, so every link keeps
    its pose relative to every other. The shoulder axis then sits 114.0 mm above
    the frame, 0.5 mm off I2RT's 113.5 mm: the residual difference between
    MuJoCo Menagerie's meshes and I2RT's CAD-aligned ones, left alone here.
    """
)
over "i2rt_yam"
{
    over "Geometry"
    {
        over "arm"
        {
            point3f physics:centerOfMass = (0, 0, 0.036)

            over "model2"
            {
                double3 xformOp:translate = (0, 0, 0.0094)
            }

            over "Capsule"
            {
                double3 xformOp:translate = (0, 0, 0.036)
            }

            over "link_1"
            {
                double3 xformOp:translate = (0, 0, 0.0731)

                over "joint1"
                {
                    point3f physics:localPos0 = (0, 0, 0.0731)
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
